WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.840
All right, I want to do a quick demonstration
for what I think is the best setup for the

00:06.840 --> 00:10.800
Work Louder Creator Micro 2.

00:10.800 --> 00:15.880
For me, I use the Claude Desktop and ChatGPT
desktop apps all the time.

00:15.880 --> 00:17.320
I use it for coding.

00:17.320 --> 00:24.520
I often switch between Claude Chat, Claude Code,
ChatGPT, and Codex all the time every day.

00:24.520 --> 00:28.400
And if you want a hands-off experience,
you can use this.

00:28.400 --> 00:35.400
I created a helper app that you can download
off of my GitHub, completely free, that allows

00:35.400 --> 00:49.200
you to quickly do things like change to Chat,
Codex, ChatGPT, and back to Claude Code.

00:49.200 --> 00:56.920
It is really flexible, easy, gives you a whole set of,
I think, the best set of keys that's

00:56.920 --> 01:04.920
out there for working completely hands-free,
everything from approval, denial, changing

01:04.920 --> 01:10.280
the model, doing dictation, submission, new line.

01:10.280 --> 01:21.360
The joystick gives you access to select all,
paste, tab, and a standard copy.

01:21.360 --> 01:30.280
You can also click the dial to search past chats,
create new chats, and stop activity.

01:30.280 --> 01:35.200
This works the same across
all four different form factors.

01:35.200 --> 01:37.800
Makes it really flexible and easy to use.
